cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results, please cite them as below."
title: "A counterexample to Davidson's Conjecture 4.3: a non-3-colourable monomial Cayley graph with an algebraic noninteger direction parameter"
authors:
  - family-names: "Çam"
    given-names: "Efe"
version: "1"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
url: "https://github.com/the-arma-of-owl/davidson-conjecture-4-3-counterexample"
repository-code: "https://github.com/the-arma-of-owl/davidson-conjecture-4-3-counterexample"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
abstract: >-
  For every root alpha of an explicit degree-12 polynomial with leading
  coefficient 2, the unit-distance graph Cay(Z[alpha], {±alpha^n : n >= 0})
  has chromatic number 4. This disproves Conjecture 4.3 of Davidson
  (arXiv:2610.09474), which predicts that three colours suffice whenever
  alpha is an algebraic noninteger. The repository contains an exact
  75,530-node infeasibility certificate with rational Farkas multipliers, a
  checker, and two independent referee reports.
keywords:
  - graph colouring
  - chromatic number
  - unit-distance graphs
  - Cayley graphs
  - Hadwiger–Nelson problem
  - counterexample
